smart.fm is a graduated recall flashcard website, and audio enhances
memory and encourages proper pronunciation. However, it doesn't
support mass upload of mp3s, but *does* have built-in text-to-speech
for a number of langauges.

A list of all gismu and their oblique forms can be found on this
spreadsheet, the working document (with wiki editting privileges) for
a the original gismu deck for smart.fm.

http://tinyurl.com/smartfmgismu

It would still require manual uploading, but if you could make 6000+
recordings, it would certainly be faster than manual recording, which
has been the only other alternative. And actually, since it appears
there are no mass uploads of any form on smart.fm, it would be just as
fast as tricking the polish voice into speaking lojban.

